 = () => {};\nwindow.$RefreshSig$ = () => (type) => type;</script>','The application appears to be a modern web application. If you need to explore it automatically then the Ajax Spider may well be more effective than the standard one.','This is an informational alert and so no changes are required.','OWASP_ZAP','POTENTIAL','2026-10-28 18:40:48.025775','10109','Medium','','-1','-1'),(349,29,'MISSING_CONTENT_TYPE_OPTIONS','LOW','http://host.docker.internal:5173/@vite [x-content-type-options]','X-Content-Type-Options Header Missing','The Anti-MIME-Sniffing header X-Content-Type-Options was not set to \'nosniff\'. This allows older versions of Internet Explorer and Chrome to perform MIME-sniffing on the response body, potentially causing the response body to be interpreted and displayed as a content type other than the declared content type. Current (early 2014) and legacy versions of Firefox will use the declared content type (if one is set), rather than performing MIME-sniffing.','Ensure that the application/web server sets the Content-Type header appropriately, and that it sets the X-Content-Type-Options header to \'nosniff\' for all web pages.\nIf possible, ensure that the end user uses a standards-compliant and modern web browser that does not perform MIME-sniffing at all, or that can be directed by the web application/web server to not perform MIME-sniffing.','OWASP_ZAP','OBSERVED','2026-10-28 18:40:48.038811','10021','Medium','https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/internet-explorer/ie-developer/compatibility/gg622941(v=vs.85)\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/Security_Headers','693','15'),(350,34,'COOKIE_MISSING_SECURE','LOW','https://owasp.org/projects/juice-shop [Set-Cookie:owasp-locale]','Set-Cookie \'owasp-locale\' was observed on an HTTPS response without the Secure attribute. The cookie value was not retained; this configuration observation does not prove that the cookie is transmitted over an insecure connection.','Observed cookie-att