Options or a CSP frame-ancestors directive to prevent framing.','PASSIVE_HEADERS','OBSERVED','2026-10-29 05:52:07.309830',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(601,39,'MISSING_CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY','MEDIUM','https://demo.owasp-juice.shop/assets/public','Content Security Policy (CSP) Header Not Set','Content Security Policy (CSP) is an added layer of security that helps to detect and mitigate certain types of attacks, including Cross Site Scripting (XSS) and data injection attacks. These attacks are used for everything from data theft to site defacement or distribution of malware. CSP provides a set of standard HTTP headers that allow website owners to declare approved sources of content that browsers should be allowed to load on that page — covered types are JavaScript, CSS, HTML frames, fonts, images and embeddable objects such as Java applets, ActiveX, audio and video files.','Ensure that your web server, application server, load balancer, etc. is configured to set the Content-Security-Policy header.','OWASP_ZAP','OBSERVED','2026-10-29 05:52:14.276175','10038','High','https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP\nhttps://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Content_Security_Policy_Cheat_Sheet.html\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/CSP/\nhttps://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/\nhttps://web.dev/articles/csp\nhttps://caniuse.com/#feat=contentsecuritypolicy\nhttps://content-security-policy.com/','693','15'),(602,39,'MISSING_STRICT_TRANSPORT_SECURITY','LOW','https://demo.owasp-juice.shop/assets/public','Strict-Transport-Security Header Not Set','HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) is a web security policy mechanism whereby a web server declares that complying user agents (such as a web browser) are to interact with it using only secure HTTPS connections (i.e. HTTP layered over TLS/SSL). HSTS is an IETF standards track protocol and is specified in RFC 6797.','Ensure that your web server, application server, load balancer, etc. is configured to enforce Strict-Transport-Security.','OWASP_ZAP','OBSERVED','2026-10-29 05:52:14.288623','10035','High','https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/HTTP_Strict_Transport_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html\nhttps://owasp.org/www-community/Security_Headers\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_Strict_Transport_Security\nhttps://caniuse.com/stricttransportsecurity\nhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6797','319','15'),(603,39,'ZAP_TIMESTAMP_DISCLOSURE_UNIX','LOW','https://demo.owasp-juice.shop/assets/public [Reporting-Endpoints]','1793253127','A timestamp was disclosed by the application/web server. - Unix','Manually confirm that the timestamp data is not sensitive, and that the data cannot be aggregated to disclose exploitable patterns.','OWASP_ZAP','POTENTIAL','2026-10-29 05:52:14.300315','10096','Low','https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html','497','13'),(604,40,'MISSING_CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY','MEDIUM','http://testasp.vulnweb.com/ [Content-Security-Policy]','Content-Security-Policy is absent','Observed in the target HTTP response','Add a restrictive Content-Security-Policy.','PASSIVE_HEADERS','OBSERVED','2026-10-29 05:52:16.311067',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(605,40,'MISSING_CONTENT_TYPE_OPTIONS','LOW','http://testasp.vulnweb.com/ [X-Content-Type-Options]','X-Content-Type-Options is absent','Observed in the target HTTP response','Send X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff.','PASSIVE_HEADERS','OBSERVED','2026-10-29 05:52:16.323744',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(606,40,'MISSING_REFERRER_POLICY','LOW','http://testasp.vulnweb.com/ [Referrer-Policy]','Referrer-Policy is absent','Observed in the target HTTP response','Set an explicit Referrer-Policy appropriate for the application.','PASSIVE_HEADERS','OBSERVED','2026-10-29 05:52:16.335230',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(607,40,'MISSING_PERMISSIONS_POLICY','LOW','http://testasp.vulnweb.com/ [Permissions-Policy]','Permissions-Policy is absent','Observed in the target HTTP response','Restrict unnecessary browser capabilities with Permissions-Policy.','PASSIVE