t which has a Session Management Method set to \"Auto-Detect\" then this rule will change the session management to use the tokens identified.','This is an informational alert rather than a vulnerability and so there is nothing to fix.','OWASP_ZAP','POTENTIAL','2026-10-29 06:35:45.756868','10112','Medium','https://www.zaproxy.org/docs/desktop/addons/authentication-helper/session-mgmt-id/','-1','-1'),(1408,48,'ZAP_SESSION_MANAGEMENT_RESPONSE_IDENTIFIED','LOW','http://testaspnet.vulnweb.com/ [ASP.NET_SessionId]','ASP.NET_SessionId','The given response has been identified as containing a session management token. The \'Other Info\' field contains a set of header tokens that can be used in the Header Based Session Management Method. If the request is in a context which has a Session Management Method set to \"Auto-Detect\" then this rule will change the session management to use the tokens identified.','This is an informational alert rather than a vulnerability and so there is nothing to fix.','OWASP_ZAP','POTENTIAL','2026-10-29 06:35:45.764946','10112','High','https://www.zaproxy.org/docs/desktop/addons/authentication-helper/session-mgmt-id/','-1','-1'),(1409,48,'INFORMATION_DISCLOSURE_SERVER','LOW','http://testaspnet.vulnweb.com/styles.css','Microsoft-IIS/8.5','The web/application server is leaking version information via the \"Server\" HTTP response header. Access to such information may facilitate attackers identifying other vulnerabilities your web/application server is subject to.','Ensure that your web server, application server, load balancer, etc. is configured to suppress the \"Server\" header or provide generic details.','OWASP_ZAP','OBSERVED','2026-10-29 06:35:45.773030','10036','High','https://httpd.apache.org/docs/current/mod/core.html#servertokens\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/msp-n-p/ff648552(v=pandp.10)\nhttps://www.troyhunt.com/shhh-dont-let-your-response-headers/','497','13'),(1410,48,'MISSING_CONTENT_TYPE_OPTIONS','LOW','http:/